Package: dahlia-agent
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Dahlia Linux <https://github.com/Fabiy99/dahlia-linux>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-yaml, adduser, systemd, dahlia-storage (= @VERSION@), docker.io | docker-ce, docker-compose (>= 2) | docker-compose-plugin, openssl, iproute2, nftables, avahi-utils, smartmontools, hdparm, ifupdown, systemd-timesyncd | time-daemon, samba, samba-vfs-modules, nfs-kernel-server, nut-client, nut-server, restic, openssh-client, wireguard-tools, qrencode, curl
Recommends: wsdd
Description: Dahlia Linux privileged agent
 Root service on /run/dahlia/agent.sock. It accepts a fixed list of
 actions (system info, hostname, storage, jobs, updates, apps, domains),
 checks every parameter and runs the matching system command. The web UI
 uses it instead of root rights. Members of the group dahlia-agent may
 connect. Also holds the local CA, the server certificate, the app
 proxies for nginx and the mDNS aliases <app>.local.
